    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-1,\\ 7$.\n\nLet $u=\\sqrt{x^2-6x-3}\\geq0$; solve $u^2-u-2=0$ and back-substitute.",
      "worked": "Let $u=\\sqrt{x^2-6x-3}\\geq0$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-2&=u\\\\u^2-u-2&=0\\\\(u-2)(u+1)&=0\\\\u&=2\\text{ or }-1.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $u=-1$ because $u\\geq0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-6x-3&=4\\\\x^2-6x-7&=0\\\\(x-7)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=7\\text{ or }-1.\\end{align*}$$\nFor both values, the original left side is $2$ and the right side is $\\sqrt4=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
